------------------------------------------------------------------------
-- Presentations of groups
--
-- The two colours of a control, given completeness on at most eight
-- wires, in the calculus with the schema.
--
-- A circuit controlled by wire 0 and one controlled by its negation
-- (ctrl⁻ C = X • ctrl C • X) commute, and a circuit one wire up is its
-- two controlled versions.  Both reduce to single gates, `opp` and
-- `split`.  When one of two gates is at the bottom of the circuit or
-- just above it, its gadget is a closed word on at most five wires; the
-- other gate is brought down to it by CtrlMove.move, whose cycle passes
-- the closed gadget and X on wire 0 (Placement.apart), until the two are
-- a closed equation on at most eight wires, which completeness proves
-- (ColourSem.opposite-sem).  When both are higher up, FullMove moves
-- both down by the same cycle, which passes X on wire 0, and what is
-- left is the equation one width down, under an idle wire on top.  The
-- colours exchange under conjugation by X (`opp-sym`).  Whole circuits
-- follow gate by gate (`opposite`, `split-w`).  The cases of a
-- gate at the bottom are generated by gen/gen_colour.py.
------------------------------------------------------------------------

